+// Everything above is app-bound: Gecko asks the player to do things.
+// Nothing came back, so AVPlayerDecoder::NotifyMetadata and
+// ::NotifyLoad were defined with no callers at all - and without
+// metadata the element never leaves HAVE_NOTHING and paints nothing,
+// however correct the frame sitting in its VideoFrameContainer is.
+// Device captures showed exactly that: "placeholder PUBLISHED
+// 1920x1080 planes=2" and a blank screen.
+//
+// A C symbol rather than a delegate protocol, because AVPlayerDecoder.h
+// is included from HTMLMediaElement.cpp - plain C++ - and cannot carry
+// an Obj-C member. This is the same shape as MainProcessInit and
+// ChildProcessInit, which Swift already calls: defined in libxul,
+// declared in a header the GeckoView umbrella exports. (The comment
+// above about raw C symbols not linking is about the opposite
+// direction, libxul referencing the app.)
+//
+// aPlayerId is the handle createPlayerWithUrl returned. The decoder
+// that owns it is found by lookup, so a stale id after teardown
+// resolves to nothing and is ignored rather than dereferenced.
